5. LINE and LY Corporation independence notice
================================================

Liney is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, authorized by,
endorsed by, sponsored by, or officially associated with LY Corporation or
the official LINE application unless a separate written agreement says so.

Liney may use unofficial software, protocols, compatibility layers, or
libraries to communicate with LINE services. Such use may stop working, may
be restricted by LINE, and may be affected by LINE's Terms of Service or
other policies. This license does not grant permission from LINE or LY
Corporation to access or use their services.

6. Cooperation and compliance requests
=======================================

The Maintainers are willing to discuss reasonable requests concerning
branding, trademarks, security, protocol behavior, distribution, features,
advertising, official notices, licensing, compatibility, or cooperation.

After receiving and reasonably verifying a formal request from LINE, LY
Corporation, or an authorized representative, the Maintainers may publish a
Formal Compliance Notice with its scope and effective date. Depending on the
request, the Maintainers may:

* stop publishing public releases;
* stop public development or make official repositories private;
* remove or restrict affected functionality;
* change the backend or migrate to an official API or SDK;
* add an authorized notice, promotion, or advertising placement;
* continue future development privately or under different terms; or
* discontinue the project.

If a Formal Compliance Notice expressly applies to further public
redistribution of a Covered Work, You must stop further public redistribution
of the affected Covered Work, remove the affected functionality where
specified, or otherwise follow the scope of the notice. The notice does not
require You to erase historical knowledge or physically delete copies that
You already received.

This section does not retroactively change the license of a copy that was
lawfully distributed before the effective date of a Formal Compliance Notice.
It also cannot change the license of independent third-party code.

